Package: gaiaCore
Type: Package
Title: Derive Place-Based Exposures from a Gaia Database in R
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jared", "Houghtaling", email = "houghtaling@ohdsi.org", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("OHDSI GIS Working Group", role = "cph"))
Description: R interface to a Gaia database (gaiaDB, PostgreSQL with PostGIS). It connects
    directly to the database with DatabaseConnector and runs the Gaia pipeline from R: ingest
    datasets registered in the Gaia catalog, load person locations and residence histories, join
    them to geospatial sources in space and time to derive EXTERNAL_EXPOSURE rows, check the
    result, and copy it into an OMOP CDM. It also provides exposure analytics: day-weighted
    exposure over windows such as pregnancy, and confidence intervals for exposure effects that
    stay valid with few, unbalanced geographic clusters.
License: Apache License 2.0
URL: https://github.com/OHDSI/gaiaCore, https://ohdsi.github.io/gaiaCore/
BugReports: https://github.com/OHDSI/gaiaCore/issues
